						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3707">Capias</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">4/30/2002 - 11:00 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2989">Capias Maximus</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														BB is fun but the trains are crazy.  You guys are the right level to go hunt in the Warrens too, if ya want.  I did both of those in my newbie days, and I found the Warrens more fun than BB and less crowded.  Loot seemed to be better too, but then again you twinks prolly don't care about loot.  :)						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3548">olthar</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">4/30/2002 - 11:47 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2836">Olthar Othlinden</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2837">Tylendil</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														LoL, I, WAY long ago... like in the days that jewlers and blacksmiths made GOOD money off silver jewlery and banded armor played in BB. Offtime was 10 to 20 people, at peak there was upwards of 40 people in the zone... everything was camped. As for trains... well we are AoE, we LOVE trains. There was this one train that happened that we tried to kill but tanky (a ranger) could not hold agro so I died... and the trainer never zoned... we also KS'd a full group fo 10 to 15 by mistake (with their permission cause they &quot;needed our help) at level 10.<br />
<br />
As for the warrens I was thinking about trying it around 14 or maybe 20... It looks like it very diverse levelwise with lots in the upper mid 20's almost like unrest. <br />
<br />
BTW any input of Zones would be appreciated, we like trainy zones with lotsa agro. current plan is <br />
<br />
BB till 12<br />
CB tr till 14/15<br />
Unrest yard trash 14/15-17/18<br />
open for suggestion<br />
Unrest (not basement) 20-23 or so<br />
open to suggestion<br />
LGUK 35 to 40 or so<br />
SolB 40 till sometime<br />
<br />
we also gonna hit mistmoore somewhere in there.						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
